 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Sounds like the chain needs cleaning and oiling. Wear also shows up as skipping, especially in the middle. Of course. With a slipping chain, you can give it a short re oil while you have it off. Drop in fresh chain when you swap it. There' be a small gear on the frame where the chain comes off. Stick a finger in it and turn it while you follow with our eyes. Turn it as if you were changing direction, turn it. Then it' probably worn needs replacing. You can split with an old chain in box at shop and ask for it. Or you can use a tool that attaches to the derailer ear and does all the work for you.",
